Ava (docs): Heads-up — I found a small but confusing gap in the error reference around context-fallback behavior when the model returns a 429 + partial content. Docs currently just say 'use fallback', but we need a short example showing: detect 429, trim older history, retry with exponential backoff and preserve user-visible continuity. Can someone help draft a compact SDK snippet we can land in the troubleshooting page?

Sam (sdk): I can draft the JS and Python snippets. Quick Q: do we recommend trimming N tokens or dropping whole messages? I think a message-level heuristic (drop oldest messages until length < X) is friendlier.

Marcus (eng-runtime): Agreed on message-level trimming. Backend also surfaces `retry-after` but it can be noisy. Best practice: honor `Retry-After` if >= 1s, otherwise exponential backoff with capped jitter. Also add a note about keeping conversation idempotent if stateful ops are present.

Priya (devex): We should include localized short strings for the UX example (en/es/fr). I can prod i18n for two short lines. Where will the snippet live? docs/troubleshooting/error-reference.md?

Ava (docs): Yes, error-reference is the right place. Keep the snippet < 20 lines. People skim these pages. Also we should link to the SDK retry util in the SDK repo.

Sam (sdk): Draft JS snippet — message-level trim + backoff (first pass):

```js
// quick fallback: drop oldest messages until under token window
async function sendWithFallback(client, convo, opts = {}) {
  let tries = 0;
  while (tries < 4) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ conversation: convo });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429) {
        // trim history, honor Retry-After
        const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
        if (retryAfter >= 1) await sleep(retryAfter * 1000);
        else await sleep(Math.pow(2, tries) * 250 + Math.random() * 100);
        // drop oldest message until under target length
        while (tokenCount(convo) > (opts.targetTokens || 3000)) convo.shift();
        tries++;
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries reached');
}
```

Sam (sdk): I'll shorten and add Python pair.

Marcus (eng-runtime): Two suggestions: 1) add a note to avoid trimming system prompts. 2) show how to detect "partial content" responses — log `err.partialResponse` if we return partial data.

Ava (docs): Good call. We'll include a callout: "Do not trim or drop system/instruction messages." Also mention logging `partialResponse` to help users reconcile state.

Priya (devex): For i18n: I'll provide translations for two UI strings: 'Trying a trimmed context…' and 'Retrying request after backoff'. I'll attach them in the PR.

